1
00:00:13,888 --> 00:00:16,933
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:37,704 --> 00:00:39,706
It might have been a memory, not a dream.

3
00:00:43,501 --> 00:00:45,378
If Jang Tae-ha's really a gangster,

4
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:48,256
this might also

5
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:51,217
have something to do with him.

6
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:56,597
Isn't it enough you've ruined your life
with violence already?

7
00:00:56,598 --> 00:01:00,601
Now you want to drag Pil-seung
into that fiery hell with you?

8
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:01,727
Not my boy.

9
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:03,437
I won't let you!

10
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:04,522
Mrs. Pang!

11
00:01:05,815 --> 00:01:07,567
No matter how angry you are,

12
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:11,446
there are things you just don't say.

13
00:01:12,197 --> 00:01:13,363
Everything else aside,

14
00:01:13,364 --> 00:01:16,451
how can you do this when you know
why Tae-ha went down that path?

15
00:01:18,411 --> 00:01:21,289
I also won't stand by
and watch my boy get hurt.

16
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:25,542
I'm sorry we didn't tell you sooner
about Pil-seung,

17
00:01:25,543 --> 00:01:28,546
but if you want to blame or sue anyone,
blame me, the head coach.

18
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:31,633
Don't take it out on Tae-ha!

19
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:39,015
You're right.

20
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:42,351
I went too far.

21
00:01:42,352 --> 00:01:46,480
It's not that I don't know
what you've been through.

22
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:49,191
I just lost my temper
out of concern for my boy.

23
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:52,319
And I know that not all boxers
become gangsters,

24
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:55,531
but it's easier to fall in with those guys
than other jobs.

25
00:01:55,532 --> 00:02:00,703
I was scared that those punks
might start eyeing my kid.

26
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:04,289
What kind of mother would want that?

27
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:08,503
Please try to understand me, Tae-ha.

28
00:02:12,590 --> 00:02:14,007
Let's go. Come on.

29
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:15,008
Wait, Mom.

30
00:02:15,009 --> 00:02:16,135
Oh, shut it.

31
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:17,595
Mom, please.

32
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:44,414
Ms. Go.

33
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:48,917
Ms. Go.

34
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:50,712
Whoa! Hey, what?

35
00:02:54,090 --> 00:02:55,716
You scared me.

36
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:57,135
Didn't you see me?

37
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:04,559
Are you okay?

38
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:18,448
Are you…

39
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:21,784
okay?

40
00:03:23,786 --> 00:03:26,998
You know I can take a hit.
I'm just worried about Pil-seung.

41
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:30,627
What, you think he goes down easy?

42
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:35,465
He's probably butting heads with his mom,
going a few rounds.

43
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:43,306
Fancy a drink?

44
00:03:52,065 --> 00:03:52,899
I should go home.

45
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:56,736
All right.

46
00:03:57,570 --> 00:04:01,032
It's a good thing you have someone at home
on a day like this.

47
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:03,701
The warmth of someone being home.

48
00:04:04,744 --> 00:04:06,120
It makes a difference.

49
00:04:08,706 --> 00:04:09,540
I'll get going.

50
00:04:19,008 --> 00:04:22,135
<i>This morning, the ceremony
for the Irang-dong development project</i>

51
00:04:22,136 --> 00:04:26,849
<i>was attended by Gangju City officials
and Mirae Eden Company representatives.</i>

52
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:31,478
<i>This project is a joint effort between
Gangju City and Mirae Eden Company,</i>

53
00:04:31,479 --> 00:04:36,025
<i>and the plan is to complete
the development in three phases by 2029.</i>

54
00:04:36,526 --> 00:04:39,611
<i>Though the blueprint for this project
was presented in 2020,</i>

55
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:43,824
<i>it was effectively halted
due to the real estate market downturn.</i>

56
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:46,201
<i>But earlier this year,
the development area was…</i>

57
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:47,453
Go Eun-sae.

58
00:04:51,374 --> 00:04:54,002
Drink this. It'll help you calm down.

59
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,763
Do you still not believe Tae-ha?

60
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:18,901
I believed him

61
00:05:20,236 --> 00:05:21,195
a little bit.

62
00:05:23,865 --> 00:05:26,366
In the midst of this absurd situation,

63
00:05:26,367 --> 00:05:27,577
there were moments

64
00:05:28,286 --> 00:05:30,621
when he seemed sincere.

65
00:05:31,539 --> 00:05:33,166
Sorry I don't express myself well.

66
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:36,169
You're the only woman I've ever liked,

67
00:05:37,587 --> 00:05:39,922
so I don't really know how.

68
00:05:41,507 --> 00:05:43,968
He wasn't exactly my ideal type,

69
00:05:44,886 --> 00:05:47,846
but he didn't seem like
a bad person either.

70
00:05:47,847 --> 00:05:50,058
I never knew she was so pretty.

71
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:59,567
But it turns out he's a gangster.

72
00:06:00,276 --> 00:06:03,029
And everything he said to me was a lie.

73
00:06:03,529 --> 00:06:06,490
Apparently, my name isn't even Go Eun-sae.

74
00:06:06,491 --> 00:06:07,533
It's Go Ji-won.

75
00:06:08,117 --> 00:06:08,951
Sorry?

76
00:06:12,663 --> 00:06:15,123
I don't know where to start
questioning things again,

77
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:17,919
or why Jang Tae-ha lied to me
about all of this,

78
00:06:18,419 --> 00:06:20,463
and what I'm supposed to do now.

79
00:06:22,173 --> 00:06:23,674
I don't know anything anymore.

80
00:06:28,679 --> 00:06:29,847
I'm scared.

81
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:34,227
Go Eun-sae!

82
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,773
Go Eun-sae!

83
00:06:40,274 --> 00:06:41,359
Eun-sae…

84
00:06:48,699 --> 00:06:49,699
Hello?

85
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:51,035
It's me, Min Su-ji.

86
00:06:53,413 --> 00:06:56,164
Right. I can't really talk right now…

87
00:06:56,165 --> 00:06:57,458
<i>Are you looking for Ms. Go?</i>

88
00:07:10,304 --> 00:07:11,222
Is she here?

89
00:07:12,140 --> 00:07:12,974
Yes.

90
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:17,395
I heard her telling Gi-jun
that she found out you're a gangster.

91
00:07:18,187 --> 00:07:21,273
And that her name is Go Ji-won,
not Go Eun-sae.

92
00:07:21,274 --> 00:07:23,484
She said she saw
her friend's social media.

93
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:26,696
What's going on?

94
00:07:27,196 --> 00:07:30,700
Is she really your girlfriend?

95
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:32,910
Now, then…

96
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:37,414
- What should we do?
- Sorry?

97
00:07:37,415 --> 00:07:40,375
I understand your situation,
but that doesn't mean…

98
00:07:40,376 --> 00:07:43,670
I can't exactly let you crash at my place.

99
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:47,925
And I can't lend you money for a place
to stay, since you can't pay me back.

100
00:07:48,426 --> 00:07:49,342
Doctor.

101
00:07:49,343 --> 00:07:50,510
Yes?

102
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:51,971
You don't have many

103
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:54,723
friends, do you?

104
00:07:54,724 --> 00:07:56,309
No, I guess I don't.

105
00:07:59,353 --> 00:08:02,606
I was just joking to cheer you up.
Come on.

106
00:08:02,607 --> 00:08:03,858
You were being serious.

107
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:08,070
Well, I'm sorry.

108
00:08:12,617 --> 00:08:13,743
Jang Tae-ha.

109
00:08:17,955 --> 00:08:20,290
I'll explain everything, so let's go home.

110
00:08:20,291 --> 00:08:23,002
How can I trust a thug and go with him?

111
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,633
You should trust what you've experienced.

112
00:08:29,383 --> 00:08:31,010
Has he ever been a threat to you?

113
00:08:32,094 --> 00:08:34,889
Has he ever threatened you,
used violence, or extorted you?

114
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:40,228
If not, then Tae-ha isn't a thug to you.

115
00:08:40,728 --> 00:08:41,646
He's just

116
00:08:42,522 --> 00:08:44,106
an ordinary man, isn't he?

117
00:08:57,411 --> 00:08:58,329
Let's talk outside.

118
00:09:23,145 --> 00:09:25,272
- Go Eun-sae.
- But I'm not Go Eun-sae.

119
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:26,523
I'm Go Ji-won, aren't I?

120
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:29,860
Go Ji-won is your legal name.
Eun-sae is the name your mother gave you.

121
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:34,531
Are you getting caught up
in your own lies? My mother?

122
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:35,991
You said I was an orphan.

123
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:39,411
Your mother left you at an orphanage
right after you were born.

124
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:41,122
The orphanage head only realized

125
00:09:41,622 --> 00:09:44,458
after registering your birth
under the name Go Ji-won

126
00:09:45,376 --> 00:09:48,337
that your name was Go Eun-sae
in your mother's maternity notebook.

127
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:52,174
You liked the name Go Eun-sae better.

128
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:55,885
You said she wouldn't have given

129
00:09:55,886 --> 00:09:58,347
such a pretty name
to a baby she didn't love.

130
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:01,767
You didn't even resent her
for abandoning you.

131
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:20,410
And the designer goods?
I saw pictures of me and my friend.

132
00:10:20,411 --> 00:10:22,787
I was dressed from head to toe
in designer items.

133
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:26,626
Then why don't I have anything like that
in my closet or shoe rack?

134
00:10:27,543 --> 00:10:29,252
You got rid of them when we moved.

135
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:30,963
- Why?
- I never asked why.

136
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:42,642
I…

137
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:51,067
I'm sorry that I was…

138
00:10:54,945 --> 00:10:55,780
a gangster.

139
00:10:58,532 --> 00:11:00,409
I was too ashamed to tell you.

140
00:11:03,621 --> 00:11:07,583
If I'd known you were a thug,
I wouldn't have believed a word you said.

141
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:10,044
If I know anything,

142
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:14,756
it's that I'd never,
not in this life or any other,

143
00:11:14,757 --> 00:11:17,468
fall for some lowlife gangster.

144
00:11:21,389 --> 00:11:22,806
I don't do that anymore.

145
00:11:22,807 --> 00:11:25,393
I won't ever use my fists
outside the ring anymore.

146
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:27,644
I promise.

147
00:11:27,645 --> 00:11:29,021
No, forget it.

148
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:32,816
Just why are you putting on this act
to keep me here?

149
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:35,444
What in the world do you want from me?

150
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:38,197
Nothing else.

151
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:42,118
Just don't disappear without a word.

152
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:45,079
Just stay out of danger.

153
00:11:45,579 --> 00:11:46,914
Just…

154
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:50,251
Just stay safe.

155
00:11:56,674 --> 00:11:58,049
Why are you overreacting?

156
00:11:58,050 --> 00:12:01,262
How would you know
if he's really Ms. Go's boyfriend?

157
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:04,681
He <i>is</i> her boyfriend.

158
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:07,893
Is she really your girlfriend?

159
00:12:09,228 --> 00:12:10,229
Is Eun-sae okay?

160
00:12:11,397 --> 00:12:13,023
- What?
- Has she been crying?

161
00:12:13,524 --> 00:12:14,358
Is she hurt?

162
00:12:26,162 --> 00:12:26,996
Go inside.

163
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:28,914
Ms. Go is fine.

164
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:36,254
Do you remember when we went to Yeosu,
and I left the hotel after we argued?

165
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:37,964
Why are you bringing that up now?

166
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:40,550
Was it right to ghost me for hours
because you were mad?

167
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:41,635
I got lost back then.

168
00:12:42,636 --> 00:12:46,432
I was just gonna cool off, then go back,
but you know I get lost easily.

169
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:50,519
I was in an unfamiliar city,
and I'd left my phone behind.

170
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:52,896
I was terrified.

171
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:55,690
When I got back to the hotel
after wandering for hours,

172
00:12:55,691 --> 00:12:59,403
you asked if I was happy I'd win
by making you worry.

173
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:06,786
Perhaps the one
who was never really a boyfriend

174
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:08,996
isn't Tae-ha,

175
00:13:09,955 --> 00:13:11,165
but you.

176
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:52,455
PARK HYO-JIN
HYOGENIE_1227

177
00:13:52,456 --> 00:13:54,707
HI. THIS IS JI-WON.
YOU'RE MY FRIEND, HYO-JIN, RIGHT?

178
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:56,252
Please read it.

179
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:59,672
Please read it and get back to me.

180
00:14:08,889 --> 00:14:12,517
<i>Hey, hey, don't run</i>

181
00:14:12,518 --> 00:14:16,564
<i>You'll only get hungrier</i>

182
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:21,609
<i>This heart-aching road of the barley hump…</i>

183
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:23,361
Hey there, Song-wol.

184
00:14:23,362 --> 00:14:25,321
These are dried persimmons.

185
00:14:25,322 --> 00:14:28,242
Put them in the freezer
and eat them with your grandma.

186
00:14:30,911 --> 00:14:35,791
<i>How did you ever live through those days?</i>

187
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:41,170
<i>Mother's sorrow</i>

188
00:14:41,171 --> 00:14:46,093
<i>Endless days of living on roots and bark</i>

189
00:14:46,677 --> 00:14:52,307
- Have you been well, ma'am?
<i>- As those times fade into the wind</i>

190
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:56,394
- I haven't been able to visit you lately.
<i>- Mother's sorrow, buried…</i>

191
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:59,273
Are you happy that Tae-ha moved down here?

192
00:15:01,609 --> 00:15:02,443
Yes, ma'am.

193
00:15:07,072 --> 00:15:09,909
I'm so sorry.

194
00:15:11,535 --> 00:15:14,705
I said something
I shouldn't have to Tae-ha.

195
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:19,752
Despite knowing why he ended up like that

196
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:24,423
and everything you went through
to raise him,

197
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:28,218
I was blinded by my love for my own child.

198
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,722
So I drove a nail

199
00:15:32,222 --> 00:15:34,642
into poor Tae-ha's heart.

200
00:15:41,899 --> 00:15:45,110
Even though I have two children of my own,

201
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:48,572
and I've grown older,

202
00:15:50,199 --> 00:15:51,742
I still have a long way to go…

203
00:15:53,869 --> 00:15:56,372
before I can call myself a true adult.

204
00:16:02,836 --> 00:16:06,382
I'll make sure to prepare
the grandest of celebrations

205
00:16:06,882 --> 00:16:08,801
for your 80th birthday.

206
00:16:09,593 --> 00:16:14,974
I know that couldn't possibly
make up for my mistake, but still.

207
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:18,811
Please go… a little easy on me.

208
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:31,156
You're telling me to stop whining
and shut up, right?

209
00:16:34,535 --> 00:16:36,787
Please stay with us for a long time.

210
00:16:37,955 --> 00:16:40,374
Until this fool, Pang Hui-ja,
finally grows up.

211
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:05,983
<i>It's me, Hyo-jin.</i>

212
00:17:07,317 --> 00:17:09,360
<i>I'm texting after seeing your DM.</i>

213
00:17:09,361 --> 00:17:10,529
<i>Let's meet.</i>

214
00:17:13,032 --> 00:17:15,451
It's okay now. I'm okay.

215
00:17:39,975 --> 00:17:41,268
HONG DO-YEOP

216
00:17:42,102 --> 00:17:43,187
Hi, Coach.

217
00:17:45,981 --> 00:17:47,024
Who's here?

218
00:17:50,986 --> 00:17:52,071
Something's come up.

219
00:17:52,988 --> 00:17:55,114
These are Grandma's favorite playlists.

220
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:56,992
Give them to Mrs. Pang at the party.

221
00:17:57,910 --> 00:17:59,035
What?

222
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:01,330
Her only grandson is skipping her party?

223
00:18:03,707 --> 00:18:05,501
She'll need these, so make sure you go.

224
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:07,461
Go there and stay put.

225
00:18:13,008 --> 00:18:14,134
What's with him?

226
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:17,471
What's more important than his grandma?

227
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:37,032
Sir!

228
00:18:37,783 --> 00:18:39,325
It's me, Gang-rok!

229
00:18:39,326 --> 00:18:40,661
Have you been well?

230
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:10,606
Sir, they sliced my Achilles' heel.

231
00:19:10,607 --> 00:19:12,526
If you leave, they usually cut off both,

232
00:19:13,235 --> 00:19:16,113
but I'm such a small fry
that they let me off with one.

233
00:19:19,825 --> 00:19:22,451
You were like a father to me.

234
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:25,622
Why would I stay in Eden
when my dad's not there?

235
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:29,792
How did you find me?

236
00:19:29,793 --> 00:19:32,421
Ages ago, we drank together,
just the two of us.

237
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:35,798
You got drunk
and told me about your hometown.

238
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:39,385
You said you wanted to go back
to the boxing gym there when you retired.

239
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:42,222
I looked it up,
and there's only one boxing gym in Gujin.

240
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:49,521
I must ask…

241
00:19:52,149 --> 00:19:53,066
Sir,

242
00:19:54,318 --> 00:19:55,736
did you save Prosecutor Go?

243
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:02,951
I saw her earlier,

244
00:20:03,535 --> 00:20:04,912
very much alive.

245
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:11,460
CONGRATULATIONS ON
MS. GO YEON-HONG'S 80TH BIRTHDAY

246
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:16,423
Nice!

247
00:20:22,179 --> 00:20:24,055
Here.

248
00:20:24,056 --> 00:20:25,264
There you go.

249
00:20:25,265 --> 00:20:27,600
All right, here goes!

250
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:31,062
I was told to give this to Mrs. Pang.

251
00:20:31,063 --> 00:20:33,357
They're songs Grandma likes.

252
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:36,108
I'll get going, then.

253
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:37,485
Hang on, lady.

254
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:39,821
Where are you going? Eat before you go.

255
00:20:40,697 --> 00:20:41,614
It's okay.

256
00:20:41,615 --> 00:20:42,741
Hold on.

257
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:46,661
Aren't you her granddaughter-in-law?

258
00:20:46,662 --> 00:20:49,330
First, you show up fashionably late.

259
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:52,417
And now what?
You're gonna show your face and leave?

260
00:20:53,794 --> 00:20:55,795
I'm not her granddaughter-in-law.

261
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:58,589
Sure, you haven't had a wedding yet,

262
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:01,677
but you're practically her family.

263
00:21:04,012 --> 00:21:05,514
- I'll get going.
- What?

264
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:08,934
- I said eat before you go.
- I said I don't want to.

265
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:13,855
You shouldn't go on an empty stomach.
At least eat this before you go.

266
00:21:14,773 --> 00:21:15,816
Oh my!

267
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:22,989
<i>Go Ji-won!</i>

268
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:25,992
I said I'll make you eat gochujang
if you leave food, didn't I?

269
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:26,952
Eat it!

270
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:29,745
Eat! I said eat!

271
00:21:29,746 --> 00:21:31,080
Open!

272
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:33,374
Open your mouth! Wide!

273
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:34,251
<i>Open!</i>

274
00:21:35,627 --> 00:21:38,255
Have you lost all your manners?

275
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:42,675
Hey, you can make a scene,
but there are lines you don't cross.

276
00:21:42,676 --> 00:21:45,387
She did that so you wouldn't go hungry.

277
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:50,057
Yeah, but… did I ever say I was hungry?

278
00:21:50,058 --> 00:21:51,768
Did I say I wanted to eat?

279
00:21:52,561 --> 00:21:56,022
People in the countryside might think
that's how you show affection,

280
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:58,190
but it's only affection if it's welcome.

281
00:21:58,191 --> 00:22:01,153
Forcing food on someone
who doesn't want to eat

282
00:22:01,778 --> 00:22:03,738
is torture.

283
00:22:03,739 --> 00:22:05,240
What? Torture?

284
00:22:06,616 --> 00:22:08,660
Hey, don't you have parents?

285
00:22:09,453 --> 00:22:12,205
Didn't your parents teach you
to be respectful?

286
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:15,000
No.

287
00:22:15,834 --> 00:22:19,087
Apparently, I don't have any parents
and grew up in an orphanage.

288
00:22:20,213 --> 00:22:22,799
- What's going on?
- What's happening?

289
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:24,675
What?

290
00:22:24,676 --> 00:22:26,678
But what difference
would parents have made?

291
00:22:27,262 --> 00:22:30,849
You have parents, and I don't,
yet we're being equally disrespectful.

292
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:35,853
I should seriously knock some sense
into that thick head of yours!

293
00:22:35,854 --> 00:22:39,649
I could also speak rudely to you,
but I'm holding back.

294
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:45,530
You should know that, at the very least,
compared to everyone here,

295
00:22:46,114 --> 00:22:48,742
I have a certain level of class and grace,

296
00:22:49,284 --> 00:22:50,869
so I'm letting this slide.

297
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:56,333
So what brings someone of such class
to the countryside?

298
00:22:58,210 --> 00:22:59,669
That's why I'm leaving.

299
00:23:00,420 --> 00:23:03,090
Because I can't bear to stay
in this low-class village

300
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:05,550
for another day.

301
00:23:07,511 --> 00:23:08,803
- Look at her.
- Ms. Go.

302
00:23:08,804 --> 00:23:11,098
- Let her go.
- That brat! Good heavens.

303
00:23:13,725 --> 00:23:15,559
Hui-ja, just let it go.

304
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:16,937
Just let her go.

305
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:19,439
Yeah, why wait until tomorrow?

306
00:23:31,243 --> 00:23:32,285
To Seoul, please.

307
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:41,335
I thought that was just like you, sir.

308
00:23:41,336 --> 00:23:45,507
The man I served all this time
has always been above taking a life.

309
00:23:47,050 --> 00:23:49,927
So does Prosecutor Go live here now?

310
00:23:49,928 --> 00:23:53,432
Has she given up being a prosecutor?
Is it to stay off the chairman's radar?

311
00:23:55,016 --> 00:23:57,060
- Gang-rok.
- Yes, sir?

312
00:23:58,437 --> 00:23:59,855
Why are you here?

313
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:06,360
I want to live here too.

314
00:24:06,361 --> 00:24:09,113
I don't care what we do.
I just want to be with you.

315
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:10,657
Please take me in.

316
00:24:33,054 --> 00:24:34,890
There's something you don't know.

317
00:24:36,391 --> 00:24:37,308
Sorry?

318
00:24:37,309 --> 00:24:39,478
Taking someone's life

319
00:24:41,188 --> 00:24:42,314
is not beneath me.

320
00:24:47,819 --> 00:24:49,738
When it comes to protecting my people,

321
00:24:50,322 --> 00:24:51,490
nothing's beneath me.

322
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:56,995
That means that if you came here
with a hidden agenda…

323
00:25:00,373 --> 00:25:02,125
I <i>will</i> kill you.

324
00:25:05,086 --> 00:25:06,254
I don't have one.

325
00:25:07,380 --> 00:25:08,507
Please believe me.

326
00:25:19,643 --> 00:25:21,770
DO JEONG-HWA

327
00:25:23,647 --> 00:25:24,481
Hello.

328
00:25:29,152 --> 00:25:29,986
I'm sorry?

329
00:25:53,301 --> 00:25:54,886
I should've done this sooner.

330
00:25:56,513 --> 00:25:58,848
Now I can breathe.

331
00:26:01,810 --> 00:26:03,478
Just don't disappear without a word.

332
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:06,523
Just stay out of danger.

333
00:26:10,527 --> 00:26:11,820
No.

334
00:26:14,155 --> 00:26:14,990
You did well.

335
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:17,993
It'll all be over tomorrow.

336
00:26:18,868 --> 00:26:19,952
JANG TAE-HA
6 MISSED CALLS

337
00:26:19,953 --> 00:26:22,163
You've held up well all this time.

338
00:26:24,874 --> 00:26:26,293
Go Eun-sae!

339
00:26:28,628 --> 00:26:29,963
Go Eun-sae!

340
00:26:32,340 --> 00:26:33,717
Go Eun-sae!

341
00:26:44,561 --> 00:26:45,812
Eun-sae!

342
00:26:59,451 --> 00:27:00,577
GO EUN-SAE

343
00:27:03,663 --> 00:27:04,663
Go Eun-sae, please.

344
00:27:04,664 --> 00:27:08,417
<i>The phone is turned off.
You will be directed to voicemail.</i>

345
00:27:08,418 --> 00:27:09,586
<i>Please leave a message…</i>

346
00:27:10,170 --> 00:27:11,588
Where the hell did you go?

347
00:27:14,841 --> 00:27:16,092
If it's Seoul…

348
00:27:16,843 --> 00:27:18,136
If you went to Seoul…

349
00:27:21,264 --> 00:27:22,599
No. Please, no.

350
00:28:25,704 --> 00:28:28,248
We have so many eyes in Seoul.

351
00:28:28,873 --> 00:28:29,791
Did you think

352
00:28:31,209 --> 00:28:32,711
you'd go unseen?

353
00:28:40,385 --> 00:28:41,386
Prosecutor.

354
00:28:51,855 --> 00:28:52,689
Go Eun-sae!

355
00:29:34,898 --> 00:29:35,815
No!

356
00:30:11,601 --> 00:30:14,020
KIM GANG-ROK

357
00:30:14,521 --> 00:30:17,731
<i>Sir, I thought about it all night.</i>

358
00:30:17,732 --> 00:30:20,609
<i>If Prosecutor Go doesn't have any ID,</i>

359
00:30:20,610 --> 00:30:22,778
<i>whose name did she use
to get a phone number?</i>

360
00:30:22,779 --> 00:30:23,780
Why do you ask?

361
00:30:33,790 --> 00:30:35,208
Today's finally the day.

362
00:30:35,708 --> 00:30:38,253
Now I'll finally find out…

363
00:30:40,421 --> 00:30:41,673
the truth.

364
00:30:59,023 --> 00:30:59,858
Hyo-jin?

365
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:01,776
Yeah.

366
00:31:04,904 --> 00:31:06,948
It's me, Park Hyo-jin.

367
00:31:10,743 --> 00:31:11,870
Thanks.

368
00:31:21,546 --> 00:31:23,506
So we really are friends.

369
00:31:27,218 --> 00:31:29,262
I finally met my best friend.

370
00:31:32,015 --> 00:31:34,267
TO HYO-JIN
FROM EUN-SAE

371
00:31:36,644 --> 00:31:37,896
"Eun-sae"?

372
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:42,816
Isn't my name Go Ji-won?

373
00:31:42,817 --> 00:31:44,819
That's your legal name.

374
00:31:45,320 --> 00:31:47,238
Go Eun-sae is the name your mom gave you.

375
00:31:47,822 --> 00:31:51,534
You liked that name better,
so I called you Eun-sae sometimes.

376
00:31:52,452 --> 00:31:53,869
<i>Go Ji-won is your legal name.</i>

377
00:31:53,870 --> 00:31:56,039
Eun-sae is the name your mother gave you.

378
00:31:57,790 --> 00:31:58,917
I see.

379
00:32:00,543 --> 00:32:02,295
But do you really

380
00:32:02,879 --> 00:32:04,047
not remember anything?

381
00:32:05,340 --> 00:32:07,716
Yeah. When I opened my eyes,
I was in the hospital.

382
00:32:07,717 --> 00:32:10,219
I couldn't remember a thing.

383
00:32:10,970 --> 00:32:14,723
Then this boxing coach from the country
showed up out of the blue,

384
00:32:14,724 --> 00:32:17,267
saying that we'd been living together
for two years.

385
00:32:17,268 --> 00:32:19,020
That I was an orphan with no family.

386
00:32:20,313 --> 00:32:23,274
It was just impossible to believe.

387
00:32:24,150 --> 00:32:26,486
What did I use to do?

388
00:32:34,035 --> 00:32:35,495
What that man said…

389
00:32:40,917 --> 00:32:41,751
is all true.

390
00:32:44,170 --> 00:32:45,087
What?

391
00:32:45,088 --> 00:32:47,089
You did grow up in an orphanage,

392
00:32:47,090 --> 00:32:49,257
your boyfriend was a boxing coach,

393
00:32:49,258 --> 00:32:51,094
and you didn't have a job as such.

394
00:32:56,432 --> 00:32:59,393
Wait, but that… can't be true.

395
00:32:59,394 --> 00:33:02,981
In all your Instagram photos,
I was dressed in designer clothes.

396
00:33:06,609 --> 00:33:08,403
Who do you think bought that for you?

397
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:12,280
- What?
- Be good to your boyfriend.

398
00:33:12,281 --> 00:33:14,617
He took care of you despite who you were.

399
00:33:21,624 --> 00:33:22,750
But…

400
00:33:24,460 --> 00:33:25,545
Why…

401
00:33:26,421 --> 00:33:28,881
As my friend, why would you
talk about me like that?

402
00:33:33,761 --> 00:33:34,971
We're friends.

403
00:33:36,973 --> 00:33:37,807
Yeah.

404
00:33:38,808 --> 00:33:40,018
We…

405
00:33:42,395 --> 00:33:43,229
used to be.

406
00:33:45,273 --> 00:33:47,983
I'll get you your drink and rice.

407
00:33:47,984 --> 00:33:50,277
- Thanks.
- Can I get you anything else?

408
00:33:50,278 --> 00:33:52,822
- We're good, thanks.
- Enjoy your meal.

409
00:34:02,957 --> 00:34:04,499
- Hey, come here.
- What is it?

410
00:34:04,500 --> 00:34:06,168
Switch shoes with me.

411
00:34:06,169 --> 00:34:07,294
What?

412
00:34:07,295 --> 00:34:08,503
Forget it.

413
00:34:08,504 --> 00:34:10,715
Come on, I want my legs to look longer.

414
00:34:11,549 --> 00:34:13,300
There's a cute customer over there.

415
00:34:13,301 --> 00:34:14,135
Hurry.

416
00:34:15,261 --> 00:34:17,513
- My feet are cold.
- Why are you barefoot?

417
00:34:19,015 --> 00:34:20,849
- Hey, careful.
- I'm okay.

418
00:34:20,850 --> 00:34:22,351
- I'm going.
- Hey.

419
00:34:22,852 --> 00:34:24,687
Go Eun-sae, seriously?

420
00:34:26,939 --> 00:34:30,275
<i>We met in our early twenties
while working part-time.</i>

421
00:34:30,276 --> 00:34:32,278
<i>We clicked and quickly became friends.</i>

422
00:34:33,112 --> 00:34:34,781
Is that right?

423
00:34:35,698 --> 00:34:39,202
You're right. I am in the area, but…

424
00:34:39,702 --> 00:34:40,703
Yes.

425
00:34:41,996 --> 00:34:42,830
No, it's fine.

426
00:34:43,331 --> 00:34:45,583
Yes, understood, sir.

427
00:34:46,834 --> 00:34:51,463
I'm sorry. My boss just called me,
and I think I have to go.

428
00:34:51,464 --> 00:34:52,547
But you just got here.

429
00:34:52,548 --> 00:34:54,549
There's an important drinks thing.

430
00:34:54,550 --> 00:34:58,678
You told me to come no matter what,
so I even closed my nail salon.

431
00:34:58,679 --> 00:35:02,433
Come on, you can't compare
closing your salon to my work drinks.

432
00:35:08,981 --> 00:35:10,775
How much does your salon make in a day?

433
00:35:11,776 --> 00:35:15,446
Let's say it's 70,000 won per appointment.
I'll send you 700,000 won.

434
00:35:16,030 --> 00:35:17,781
- What?
- I'm sorry.

435
00:35:17,782 --> 00:35:18,783
See you!

436
00:35:36,801 --> 00:35:39,095
<i>But at a certain point, you changed.</i>

437
00:35:39,846 --> 00:35:42,890
What? Hyo-jin bought this?

438
00:35:43,474 --> 00:35:45,935
But this costs over five million won.

439
00:35:46,435 --> 00:35:49,230
She said she considered it for months
before buying it.

440
00:35:52,150 --> 00:35:53,985
I guess she'll be back for a refund.

441
00:35:58,197 --> 00:36:00,741
<i>Time and time again, you hurt me.</i>

442
00:36:02,827 --> 00:36:06,038
<i>You often made me feel
miserable and humiliated.</i>

443
00:36:13,212 --> 00:36:14,797
I really did that?

444
00:36:18,593 --> 00:36:21,052
It's not that I wasn't worried
when you went missing,

445
00:36:21,053 --> 00:36:23,431
but knowing that the person
who hurt me was gone

446
00:36:24,223 --> 00:36:25,141
wasn't so bad.

447
00:36:26,350 --> 00:36:29,937
Now that I've seen you're okay,
please don't contact me anymore.

448
00:36:30,646 --> 00:36:32,440
Wait. I'm sorry.

449
00:36:34,192 --> 00:36:37,360
I'm just having a hard time
believing what you're saying right now.

450
00:36:37,361 --> 00:36:40,906
There isn't a single designer item
in the house I live in right now.

451
00:36:40,907 --> 00:36:42,824
How do you explain that?

452
00:36:42,825 --> 00:36:45,536
You're not lying to me, too, are you?

453
00:36:51,375 --> 00:36:52,585
Ji-won.

454
00:36:58,716 --> 00:37:01,886
Isn't it obvious why you wouldn't have
the designer items you bought?

455
00:37:03,095 --> 00:37:04,680
You returned them.

456
00:37:06,098 --> 00:37:07,850
Or sold them because you needed money.

457
00:37:09,727 --> 00:37:10,770
That's why

458
00:37:12,063 --> 00:37:14,523
you should've known
to live within your means.

459
00:37:24,659 --> 00:37:25,910
Wait, I…

460
00:37:44,679 --> 00:37:47,348
SORRY FOR NOT OPENING THE DOOR
WHY AM I ALWAYS SO SORRY?

461
00:37:59,151 --> 00:38:01,486
At the very least,
compared to everyone here,

462
00:38:01,487 --> 00:38:04,407
I have a certain level of class and grace,

463
00:38:05,199 --> 00:38:06,617
so I'm letting this slide.

464
00:38:08,244 --> 00:38:09,829
Class? What class?

465
00:38:10,538 --> 00:38:12,039
I was the lowest of them all.

466
00:38:18,337 --> 00:38:21,965
<i>If the phone is under your name,
can't we track it?</i>

467
00:38:21,966 --> 00:38:26,470
<i>These days, they can track your phone
with your consent if you lose it.</i>

468
00:38:31,809 --> 00:38:33,436
What do I do?

469
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:41,569
I'm the worst.

470
00:39:03,758 --> 00:39:04,842
Go Eun-sae.

471
00:39:28,199 --> 00:39:30,283
Why are you on the street like this?

472
00:39:30,284 --> 00:39:31,410
What are you doing here?

473
00:39:32,078 --> 00:39:33,954
Forget it. I don't want to talk about it.

474
00:39:39,085 --> 00:39:40,586
Let's just go home.

475
00:39:48,177 --> 00:39:50,512
How could I go back there?

476
00:39:50,513 --> 00:39:54,057
I made a total mess when I left.

477
00:39:54,058 --> 00:39:59,229
I said all kinds of things
to your grandma and the ladies,

478
00:39:59,230 --> 00:40:03,234
yelling like someone
who would never come back.

479
00:40:04,443 --> 00:40:06,987
How could I go back now?

480
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:12,993
Oh my goodness.

481
00:40:16,956 --> 00:40:21,794
I'm so mad that this is all I amounted to.

482
00:40:58,289 --> 00:40:59,331
Let's eat something.

483
00:41:03,127 --> 00:41:04,253
Hey, Tae-ha.

484
00:41:05,671 --> 00:41:09,800
Does your wife use cement
instead of makeup or something?

485
00:41:10,843 --> 00:41:13,971
It's just that she has such thick skin.

486
00:41:16,307 --> 00:41:18,641
Why are you so silent?

487
00:41:18,642 --> 00:41:25,190
Right. I guess you can't talk to us ladies
who are so far beneath you.

488
00:41:25,191 --> 00:41:26,149
She just--

489
00:41:26,150 --> 00:41:29,194
Come on, you're just as bad.

490
00:41:29,195 --> 00:41:32,322
Think hard about which side to take,
you spineless dummy.

491
00:41:32,323 --> 00:41:35,451
Do you even know
what she did to your grandmother?

492
00:41:35,951 --> 00:41:40,371
If you still have that mouth of yours
that spewed out all those nasty words,

493
00:41:40,372 --> 00:41:41,874
why don't you say something?

494
00:41:42,374 --> 00:41:45,293
After ruining an 80-year-old woman's
birthday party,

495
00:41:45,294 --> 00:41:49,465
how could you have the nerve
to crawl back here?

496
00:41:50,716 --> 00:41:52,343
I told her to come.

497
00:41:57,181 --> 00:41:58,973
You did, ma'am?

498
00:41:58,974 --> 00:42:01,352
Yes, I asked her to come back.

499
00:42:04,063 --> 00:42:05,522
Hey, Song-wol.

500
00:42:05,523 --> 00:42:07,816
She's not in her right mind
right now, is she?

501
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:09,567
What if I'm not?

502
00:42:09,568 --> 00:42:12,029
Are you going to kick her out?

503
00:42:13,656 --> 00:42:15,156
Of course we wouldn't…

504
00:42:15,157 --> 00:42:18,369
I just asked my family to return.

505
00:42:18,869 --> 00:42:20,704
Do you have a problem with that?

506
00:42:24,333 --> 00:42:27,545
So leave the girl alone now.

507
00:42:28,879 --> 00:42:29,964
Okay?

508
00:43:03,163 --> 00:43:04,582
By any chance,

509
00:43:05,499 --> 00:43:09,211
did you ask your grandma to do that?

510
00:43:10,713 --> 00:43:12,715
How would I know
when she'd come to her senses?

511
00:43:16,218 --> 00:43:17,428
Then why…

512
00:43:20,848 --> 00:43:21,974
Because she's my grandma.

513
00:43:40,367 --> 00:43:43,912
I have to go to the gym real quick.

514
00:43:45,497 --> 00:43:46,582
Okay.

515
00:43:51,295 --> 00:43:54,506
I have to… go somewhere too.

516
00:44:25,245 --> 00:44:31,043
We're not just stretching and twisting
this taffy for no reason.

517
00:44:31,919 --> 00:44:35,963
We're letting air into it.

518
00:44:35,964 --> 00:44:41,178
If you keep flattening and folding
the taffy over and over,

519
00:44:41,762 --> 00:44:45,307
it forms air bubbles in the center.

520
00:44:45,891 --> 00:44:50,812
The air bubbles
make it sweeter and crumblier.

521
00:44:50,813 --> 00:44:53,649
That's how we make better taffy.

522
00:44:55,859 --> 00:44:57,861
It's the same for people.

523
00:44:58,445 --> 00:45:01,365
Not having any flaws
isn't always a good thing.

524
00:45:03,701 --> 00:45:07,746
If you end up having a few holes
for whatever reason,

525
00:45:08,330 --> 00:45:12,167
you'll find that your tough life
becomes sweeter and crumblier.

526
00:45:12,668 --> 00:45:15,838
And it'll make you a better person.

527
00:45:17,506 --> 00:45:21,009
So it's okay to be a little embarrassed.

528
00:45:21,510 --> 00:45:25,139
It's completely fine for a person
to be embarrassed once in a while.

529
00:45:36,692 --> 00:45:38,444
I'm sorry.

530
00:45:42,156 --> 00:45:43,532
I'm so sorry.

531
00:45:45,033 --> 00:45:48,328
I thought you were a lady,
but you're just a baby.

532
00:45:48,829 --> 00:45:50,330
Look at you.

533
00:46:17,191 --> 00:46:18,525
Hello.

534
00:46:26,200 --> 00:46:27,159
Tae-ha, that punk…

535
00:46:29,620 --> 00:46:32,706
He was no ordinary kid.

536
00:46:33,415 --> 00:46:35,917
In just six months of training with me,

537
00:46:35,918 --> 00:46:40,339
he swept the city, province,
and national competitions.

538
00:46:40,964 --> 00:46:46,220
In no time, he became a national athlete
and trained at Taereung.

539
00:46:49,264 --> 00:46:52,518
But then, the old lady became unwell.

540
00:46:54,186 --> 00:46:55,312
His grandmother?

541
00:46:55,979 --> 00:46:59,107
Yes. Though she's technically
not his real grandmother.

542
00:47:01,235 --> 00:47:03,277
She's not his real grandmother?

543
00:47:03,278 --> 00:47:06,864
With nowhere to go, Tae-ha's mom
stumbled into our village with a newborn,

544
00:47:06,865 --> 00:47:09,701
then died after staying at
Lady Go's house for a while.

545
00:47:10,494 --> 00:47:12,663
So the old lady raised Tae-ha.

546
00:47:15,374 --> 00:47:18,877
I thought they were family.

547
00:47:19,378 --> 00:47:21,087
They <i>are</i> family.

548
00:47:21,088 --> 00:47:23,923
Do they have to be blood-related
to be family?

549
00:47:23,924 --> 00:47:26,133
That's it! My Tae-ha, you're doing great.

550
00:47:26,134 --> 00:47:27,803
Tae-ha, don't get worked up.

551
00:47:30,180 --> 00:47:31,181
Stop!

552
00:47:31,807 --> 00:47:35,268
<i>She raised him with more care
than she would her own grandchildren.</i>

553
00:47:35,269 --> 00:47:37,270
- Wasn't I great?
- Yes!

554
00:47:37,271 --> 00:47:40,189
<i>The old lady was so warm,
showering him with endless love.</i>

555
00:47:40,190 --> 00:47:41,899
My baby, you did great.

556
00:47:41,900 --> 00:47:45,487
<i>Until then, there were no shadows
in Tae-ha's life.</i>

557
00:48:02,379 --> 00:48:05,591
TAE-HA, GRANDMA COLLAPSED
COME TO BODEUM HOSPITAL CANCER CENTER

558
00:48:07,801 --> 00:48:12,097
<i>Perhaps that's why
he wanted to save her no matter what.</i>

559
00:48:14,266 --> 00:48:17,102
<i>But the surgery and medication
cost nearly a hundred million,</i>

560
00:48:17,603 --> 00:48:19,855
<i>and Tae-ha was only 20 years old.</i>

561
00:48:21,064 --> 00:48:22,941
<i>Where could he get that kind of money?</i>

562
00:48:23,692 --> 00:48:26,444
<i>He couldn't afford it
with his training camp allowance,</i>

563
00:48:26,445 --> 00:48:29,031
<i>and his signing bonus
from the semipro team wasn't much.</i>

564
00:48:30,324 --> 00:48:31,742
And that's when

565
00:48:32,326 --> 00:48:36,496
<i>this gang called Geukrakpa
reached out to him.</i>

566
00:48:45,923 --> 00:48:47,925
<i>His grandma survived,</i>

567
00:48:48,425 --> 00:48:51,887
<i>but when she found out
how Tae-ha had saved her,</i>

568
00:48:52,846 --> 00:48:56,016
<i>she soon started to slip away.</i>

569
00:48:57,476 --> 00:48:59,436
<i>She couldn't go on living</i>

570
00:49:00,312 --> 00:49:02,272
<i>without erasing the memory of that.</i>

571
00:49:14,368 --> 00:49:18,621
<i>After Tae-ha became a gangster,
he lived like a machine.</i>

572
00:49:18,622 --> 00:49:21,166
<i>Beating people up
and breaking things on command.</i>

573
00:49:32,052 --> 00:49:34,512
<i>He lived like that for 14 years,</i>

574
00:49:34,513 --> 00:49:37,265
<i>afraid that he might have regrets
if he ever looked back.</i>

575
00:50:44,624 --> 00:50:47,586
<i>But he's always been too kind by nature.</i>

576
00:50:48,545 --> 00:50:50,881
<i>No matter how much
he tried to live like a machine,</i>

577
00:50:51,923 --> 00:50:54,009
<i>he couldn't help
but feel sick to his stomach.</i>

578
00:51:06,897 --> 00:51:07,773
That's why

579
00:51:09,649 --> 00:51:10,984
he came back.

580
00:51:16,740 --> 00:51:18,366
Tae-ha's heart

581
00:51:19,451 --> 00:51:20,494
is deeply wounded.

582
00:51:21,953 --> 00:51:23,913
A wound that will never heal

583
00:51:23,914 --> 00:51:26,458
and that will never fade.

584
00:51:27,667 --> 00:51:29,251
I don't know about anyone else,

585
00:51:29,252 --> 00:51:30,587
but you…

586
00:51:31,880 --> 00:51:36,093
I just hope you won't make
that wound any worse.

587
00:51:46,812 --> 00:51:49,147
- Excuse me.
- Sure.

588
00:51:50,440 --> 00:51:51,525
Hello.

589
00:51:52,317 --> 00:51:53,985
Yes, this is Hong's Boxing Gym.

590
00:51:55,487 --> 00:51:56,404
Sorry?

591
00:51:57,364 --> 00:51:58,490
Tae-ha?

592
00:52:00,158 --> 00:52:02,409
You're honestly blaming me for this?

593
00:52:02,410 --> 00:52:05,496
I told you that bastard
broke my side mirror and just ran off!

594
00:52:05,497 --> 00:52:06,413
Come on now.

595
00:52:06,414 --> 00:52:09,500
He said he had an emergency
and left his contact information.

596
00:52:09,501 --> 00:52:11,043
Did he not?

597
00:52:11,044 --> 00:52:13,295
Then why didn't he call me
after he was done?

598
00:52:13,296 --> 00:52:15,756
I had to call him and drag him out here!

599
00:52:15,757 --> 00:52:17,592
How is this not a hit-and-run?

600
00:52:18,176 --> 00:52:20,011
You didn't have to mess up his face.

601
00:52:20,595 --> 00:52:23,264
Violence can never be justified!

602
00:52:23,265 --> 00:52:25,142
- What the hell happened?
- There you are.

603
00:52:27,102 --> 00:52:28,145
Go Eun-sae.

604
00:52:29,354 --> 00:52:30,480
Did you get beat up?

605
00:52:31,064 --> 00:52:32,482
No, I…

606
00:52:36,236 --> 00:52:37,696
Oh, dear God.

607
00:52:38,405 --> 00:52:41,241
- Where is your family burial ground?
- What now?

608
00:52:41,825 --> 00:52:43,076
Bow in that direction. Now.

609
00:52:44,369 --> 00:52:46,454
If he's held back any less,

610
00:52:47,581 --> 00:52:50,207
you'd be joining your ancestors by now.

611
00:52:50,208 --> 00:52:51,626
What the hell are you on about?

612
00:52:52,210 --> 00:52:53,627
I'm his guardian.

613
00:52:53,628 --> 00:52:58,507
I'll replace that side mirror
with the fanciest one out there.

614
00:52:58,508 --> 00:52:59,551
Talk it out with me.

615
00:53:00,260 --> 00:53:02,344
You're laughing? You think this is funny?

616
00:53:02,345 --> 00:53:04,054
- You wanna go?
- Let's go talk.

617
00:53:04,055 --> 00:53:05,348
Do-yeop, you can't hit him.

618
00:53:31,124 --> 00:53:34,668
I thought you were a good boxer.
A former gangster.

619
00:53:34,669 --> 00:53:37,380
Couldn't you have just knocked him out
with a few punches?

620
00:53:40,467 --> 00:53:42,510
It wouldn't have taken a few.

621
00:53:43,011 --> 00:53:43,928
Just one.

622
00:53:43,929 --> 00:53:44,888
Exactly.

623
00:53:45,972 --> 00:53:48,350
So why did you let him
beat you up like this?

624
00:53:50,852 --> 00:53:52,103
I didn't get beat up.

625
00:53:52,854 --> 00:53:54,314
I was blocking, and…

626
00:54:03,698 --> 00:54:04,658
I promised you.

627
00:54:06,076 --> 00:54:06,910
What?

628
00:54:11,998 --> 00:54:14,292
I won't ever use my fists
outside the ring anymore.

629
00:54:15,710 --> 00:54:16,753
I promise.

630
00:54:29,391 --> 00:54:30,225
That's why…

631
00:54:32,727 --> 00:54:34,521
you just let him beat you up?

632
00:54:38,525 --> 00:54:39,567
Mr. Jang Tae-ha.

633
00:54:40,318 --> 00:54:41,278
Are you stupid?

634
00:54:42,445 --> 00:54:46,448
Why would you stand there and take it
when you did nothing wrong?

635
00:54:46,449 --> 00:54:48,242
You hit back in situations like this.

636
00:54:48,243 --> 00:54:49,744
You should have hit him back.

637
00:55:11,516 --> 00:55:12,726
What should I do with you?

638
00:55:17,564 --> 00:55:19,524
This must be why I liked you.

639
00:55:20,734 --> 00:55:22,444
Gangster or not,

640
00:55:23,486 --> 00:55:25,572
that must be why.

641
00:55:28,867 --> 00:55:30,160
I'm sorry.

642
00:55:33,496 --> 00:55:35,999
I'm sorry for not remembering you
and making you upset.

643
00:56:16,998 --> 00:56:18,666
OUR STICKY LOVE

644
00:57:05,296 --> 00:57:09,259
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
